  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>→</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> <br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>→</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> <br/><br/>Both C and N can donate electron pairs. Since KCN is predominantly ionic and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>  bond is more stable than  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>  bond in case of KCN, attack takes place through carbon atom.<br/><br/>AgCN is predominantly covalent hence only nitrogen pair is available for bonding resulting in formation of isocyanide."
